mail-filter (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A daemon that dies during startup now says why on FreeBSD. It writes the
    reason to stderr, and the rc.d script handed stderr to daemon(8) with -f,
    which sends it to /dev/null; the daemon cannot write to its own log file
    yet, because the path to it is in the configuration it just failed to
    read. Added -S -T to daemon(8) so startup output goes to syslog, which is
    what systemd's journal already did on Debian.

  * A failed start no longer prints the tail of the log as its diagnosis
    unless this attempt actually wrote to it. It used to show five lines from
    the previous, successful run -- the last of them announcing that the
    daemon had started -- directly underneath "failed to start".

  * "service mail_filter start" now exits non-zero when the daemon does not
    come up. rc.subr ignores the return value of start_postcmd, so the script
    knew about the failure and reported success anyway.

  * "service mail_filter configtest" and --configtest now answer the question
    that matters: can the *daemon's* user read these files? Run as root, both
    used to pass on a configuration root could read and postfix could not --
    the exact blind spot that hid the bug fixed in 1.0.1.

  * Purging the Debian package no longer deletes an administrator's own copy
    of the log. postrm removed /var/log/mail_filter.log.* , which matches
    mail_filter.log.save just as happily as logrotate's mail_filter.log.1;
    it is now .log.[0-9]* .

 -- Pavel Hlubík <phlubik@seznam.cz>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0000

mail-filter (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Configuration files are installed 0644 rather than 0640. The directory
    above them is 0750 root:postfix, so nothing outside root and the daemon
    can reach them whatever their mode -- the group bit protected nothing and
    cost something. cp preserves the mode of its source, so
    "cp mail_filter.conf.dpkg-dist mail_filter.conf" -- the obvious thing to
    do -- used to produce a file the daemon could not read.

 -- Pavel Hlubík <phlubik@seznam.cz>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0000

mail-filter (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A configuration file the daemon cannot read is now an error rather than
    silence. configparser.read() skips a file it cannot open and reports
    nothing, so a mail_filter.conf left root:wheel mode 640 -- readable by
    root, and therefore fine to --configtest -- left the daemon running on
    built-in defaults: default socket, default limits, no [mail_log], and
    loglevel INFO while the file on disk said WARNING. It looked like it
    worked, because the defaults are reasonable.

 -- Pavel Hlubík <phlubik@seznam.cz>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

mail-filter (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaged release of mail_filter, the unified Subject and body
    milter merged from the former subject_milter and body_milter.

 -- Pavel Hlubík <phlubik@seznam.cz>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0000
